      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "notes": "One stable id and one stable path for the whole pipeline. Each feature re-imports this workflow under the same id rather than adding a second one: two workflows claiming a path leaves the loser silently unregistered, and deactivating the winner does not hand the path back."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "http://media-service:8001/media/jobs",
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "url",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.url }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "callback_url",
              "value": "={{ 'http://n8n:5678/webhook-waiting/' + $execution.resumeUrl.split('/webhook-waiting/')[1] }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Start ingest",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        20,
        0
      ],
      "notes": "The host is swapped, not the path: $execution.resumeUrl is built from WEBHOOK_URL and would say localhost:5678, which inside media-service means media-service. The split keeps the execution id and any ?signature= the resume URL carries."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resume": "webhook",
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
